    {
      "segment": 1,
      "duration": 10.0,
      "text": "This paper follows two compact summaries of galaxy growth: the star-forming main sequence and the mass-metallicity relation. It measures how far JWST galaxies sit from a uniform local SDSS anchor.",
      "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
      "voice_gender": "Female",
      "synthesis_rate": "+42%",
      "raw_duration": 9.456,
      "atempo": 1.000635,
      "actual_speech_duration": 9.45,
      "trailing_room": 0.2,
      "output": "/Users/duhokim/NebulaMind/NebulaMind/.hermes/handoffs/paper-videos-20260722T121412Z/build/scaling-relations/audio/segment_01.wav"
    },
    {
      "segment": 2,
      "duration": 11.0,
      "text": "The local baseline uses about four hundred ninety thousand SDSS galaxies. The high-redshift side combines one hundred eighty NIRSpec galaxies with three thousand seven hundred forty-three MIRI and CEERS sources.",
      "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
      "voice_gender": "Female",
      "synthesis_rate": "+20%",
      "raw_duration": 10.872,
      "atempo": 1.040383,
      "actual_speech_duration": 10.45,
      "trailing_room": 0.2,
      "output": "/Users/duhokim/NebulaMind/NebulaMind/.hermes/handoffs/paper-videos-20260722T121412Z/build/scaling-relations/audio/segment_02.wav"
    },
    {
      "segment": 3,
      "duration": 12.0,
      "text": "At fixed mass, star formation is elevated by 0.77 dex near redshift 3.5 and reaches 1.94 dex beyond redshift six. That is roughly six to almost one hundred times the local rate.",
      "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
      "voice_gender": "Female",
      "synthesis_rate": "+20%",
      "raw_duration": 12.0,
      "atempo": 1.048035,
      "actual_speech_duration": 11.45,
      "trailing_room": 0.2,
      "output": "/Users/duhokim/NebulaMind/NebulaMind/.hermes/handoffs/paper-videos-20260722T121412Z/build/scaling-relations/audio/segment_03.wav"
    },
    {
      "segment": 4,
      "duration": 12.0,
      "text": "On a matched direct-Te scale, the metallicity deficits are minus 0.43, minus 0.37, and minus 0.40 dex near redshifts 4.6, 5.3, and 7.2. They do not deepen strongly.",
      "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
      "voice_gender": "Female",
      "synthesis_rate": "+35%",
      "raw_duration": 11.472,
      "atempo": 1.001921,
      "actual_speech_duration": 11.45,
      "trailing_room": 0.2,
      "output": "/Users/duhokim/NebulaMind/NebulaMind/.hermes/handoffs/paper-videos-20260722T121412Z/build/scaling-relations/audio/segment_04.wav"
    },
    {
      "segment": 5,
      "duration": 12.0,
      "text": "The default Tremonti anchor sits about 0.24 dex higher. Recomputing two hundred thousand SDSS galaxies on the Te-anchored PP04 O3N2 scale prevents the high-redshift deficit from being overstated by about 0.1 dex.",
      "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
      "voice_gender": "Female",
      "synthesis_rate": "+33%",
      "raw_duration": 11.448,
      "atempo": 0.999825,
      "actual_speech_duration": 11.45,
      "trailing_room": 0.2,
      "output": "/Users/duhokim/NebulaMind/NebulaMind/.hermes/handoffs/paper-videos-20260722T121412Z/build/scaling-relations/audio/segment_05.wav"
    },
    {
      "segment": 6,
      "duration": 13.0,
      "text": "JWST selection favors strong emission lines and high specific star formation; the local relations are extrapolated at low mass. This autonomous draft has no human clearance. It is descriptive, not validated.",
      "voice": "en-US-EmmaNeural",
      "voice_gender": "Female",
      "synthesis_rate": "+20%",
      "raw_duration": 11.832,
